 "text": "A group can make you deny what you see with your own eyes. Here's proof. In the 1950s, psychologist Solomon Asch showed people three lines. Which one matches this one? Easy. Alone, people got it wrong less than 1% of the time. But everyone else in the room was an actor. One by one, they all gave the same wrong answer. Three out of four real people went along at least once. Here's the trick. Your brain hates standing out, but when just one other person gave the right answer, going along dropped sharply. So, if you know you're right, say it. And if someone stands alone, stand with them. Follow for more mind tricks.",
